 "signature": null,
 "observations": [
  "col_left L1: the entry Barhebraeus of p. 379 goes on here.",
  "col_left L3: «’l-faraǵ» is printed with ǵ, Nallino's sign for jīm.",
  "col_left L5: «Ēliyyāh» is printed with a macron over the capital E (4.3 points wide, at the height of the capitals); the ṣ of «Bashyaṣī» has its dot below, the ī its bar (2.4 by 1.0 points).",
  "col_left L6, L10: «βασιλίσκος», «βασιλικός», «α» and «βαθμός» are Greek; the accents are acutes.",
  "col_left L9: the hyphen of «314-315» is printed as a point at mid height (1.2 by 1.0 points); the hyphen of «308-309» is printed short (2.3 points).",
  "col_left L10: «13» is printed upright. A round dot (2.2 by 1.7 points) stands under the d of «ordines», 0.9-2.6 points below the baseline; the Latin word has no letter with a dot below; not transcribed.",
  "col_left L11: the mark over the i of «al-Battānī» is a bar (2.0 by 1.1 points), as on p. 377 (on p. 374 the form al-Battāni has a dot). Measured with macron_audit.py.",
  "col_left L24: the hyphen of «{sc:vii}-{sc:viii}» is printed as a point at mid height (1.3 by 1.0 points).",
  "col_left L30, L32, L34, L36, L39, L42, L44: the marks over the i of «al-Bīrūnī», «al-Khāzinī» (the second i), «al-Mas‘ūdī», «aṣ-Ṣūfī», «Elī‘ezer», «az-Zarqālī», «mīnī» (twice) and «al-Kharaqī» are bars (1.8-2.4 by 0.8-1.1 points); the first i of «al-Khāzinī» and the i of «Ḥiyyā» have round dots (1.2-1.6 points). Measured with macron_audit.py.",
  "col_left L33: «Hibintà» is printed with a grave accent on the final a.",
  "col_left L37: «Rabiçag» is printed with a cedilla under the c.",
  "col_left L42: the ō of «Yōsēph» is the sort with its macron joined to the top of the o (the letter stands 0.7 point above the x-height; the same sort in this name on Part I p. 293 and in this index on pp. 392 and 412); the ē has a separate bar (2.6 by 1.0 points).",
  "col_left L43: «al-Ǵagh-» is printed with a capital G with an acute (Ǵ), Nallino's sign for jīm.",
  "col_right L2, L3: the ḍ of «*al-bayḍah*» and of «al-Bayḍāwī» has its dot below; the last i of «al-Bayḍāwī» has a bar (2.5 by 1.2 points).",
  "col_right L4: a round dot (1.4 by 1.6 points) under the junction of the a and the y of «Bayer», 1.0-2.5 points below the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L14: «Bēlṭĕshaṣṣar» is printed with a macron over the first e, a dot under the t, a breve over the second e and dots under both s.",
  "col_right L17: a large round speck (2.4 by 1.9 points) at mid height, far to the right of «Bereni {sc:xxviii}.», is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L19: «α» is Greek; «al-ǵawzā’» is printed with ǵ and ends with the sign of hamza.",
  "col_right L21: «Béziat» is printed with an acute over the e.",
  "col_right L22: «Siddhānta-śiromaṇi» is printed with an acute over the s (ś) and a dot under the n (ṇ).",
  "col_right L26: «Björnbo» is printed with a diaeresis on the o; its two dots are blotted together and joined to the top of the letter by a thin bridge.",
  "col_right L27: a speck (1.0 by 1.1 points) above the line after «Thābit.» is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L35: a speck (0.8 by 1.6 points) under «216 n.,» is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L40: «354 n ,» is printed with no point after n; a space stands before the comma; transcribed as printed.",
  "col_right L44: the italic t of the title (tasṭīḥ) is printed joined to «liber», and the space stands after it: «liber*t* *asṭīḥ*»; transcribed as printed. The ṭ, the ḥ and both ṣ have their dots below; the ī its bar (2.8 by 1.0 points).",
  "col_right L46: the m of «*Khuwārizmī*» is printed with its strokes apart, like ni; the final ī has its bar (3.2 by 1.2 points).",
  "col_right L46: the entry al-Bīrūnī goes on on p. 381."
 ],
